This directory is intentionally empty in source control.

Review finding ("P0 #2" — "You still ship an admin bootstrap secret inside the frontend"):
investigating that finding turned up something broader — this directory previously held a
STALE, committed Angular production build (dated weeks before the fix), containing not just the
leaked admin bootstrap secret but also several other bugs already fixed in source (hardcoded
localhost URLs, among others). Since Spring Boot serves anything here as static web content
automatically, a deployment built straight from this repo without a fresh frontend build would
have silently shipped that old, vulnerable bundle regardless of any source fixes.

The Dockerfile now builds the Angular frontend fresh and copies it here as part of every image
build (see the "Stage 0: Frontend build" section) — nothing should ever be manually committed
into this directory again. See .gitignore for the enforcement.
